ing narrative to a climax."}], "places": [{"name": "Provo, United States", "role": "Birthplace"}, {"name": "Scadrial", "role": "Setting"}, {"name": "Salt Lake City, United States", "role": "Major event location"}], "texts": [{"title": "Wikipedia: Mistborn", "type": "Reference article", "slug": "mistborn"}], "externalLinks": ["https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q268100", "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mistborn"], "tags": ["novel series", "Novels & Prose Fiction", "cause-and-effect"], "thumbnailUrl": "", "quote": "", "legacySummary": "Key lasting impacts include: Contributed to cultural heritage and knowledge transmission. Their legacy is studied through the lens of historical causation.", "historicalSignificance": {"significanceScore": 7, "significanceNarrative": "Mistborn reshaped modern fantasy literature by introducing complex characters and intricate magic systems, influencing numerous authors and adaptations.", "significanceCategory": "regional"}, "_editLog": [{"timestamp": "2026-07-30T13:07:12Z", "editorId": "gpt-4o-mini·cloud·GH#30545273640", "field": "summary", "oldValue": "Novel series by brandon sanderson Created by Brandon Sanderson.", "newValue": "Mistborn is a critically acclaimed fantasy novel series created by Brandon Sanderson, first published between 2006 and 2016. Set in a richly developed world known as Scadrial, the series explores themes of power, morality, and rebellion, resonating with readers across the globe. Sanderson's unique system of magic, known as Allomancy, which allows characters to manipulate metals for various effects, has made a profound impact on the fantasy genre, combining elements of epic storytelling with intricate world-building. The series has gained a dedicated fanbase, influencing both literature and adaptations in various media forms.

The narrative of Mistborn unfolds over a trilogy, starting with "Mistborn: The Final Empire," where a young street urchin named Vin discovers her powers and joins a band of rebels aiming to overthrow an oppressive regime ruled by the immortal Lord Ruler. This rebellion is not merely a fight against tyranny but also a deep exploration of personal identity and societal change. The subsequent books, "The Well of Ascension" and "The Hero of Ages," expand on this conflict, delving into themes of sacrifice, leadership, and the consequences of power. The intricate plot twists and character development not only enhance the storytelling but also invite readers to reflect on real-world issues of governance and morality.

